input_prompt: Explain what on-device AI means in simple terms.
INFO: Loaded OpenCL library with dlopen.


On-device AI means using artificial intelligence (AI) directly on your device, like a smartphone or tablet, instead of sending data to the cloud. Think of it like a computer doing work without needing the internet. For example, if you use a voice assistant (like Siri or Google Assistant), the AI processes your voice commands right on your phone, not on a faraway server. This keeps your data private, works faster, and uses less data. It’s great for tasks that need quick responses, like translating speech or playing games. But it’s not as powerful as cloud AI for complex tasks, so some apps still use cloud-based AI for things like high-quality photo analysis. In short, on-device AI lets your device do smart things without needing the cloud—making it faster, more private, and more efficient. 🚀✨

